  "plain": "The media owner Robert Maxwell, father of Ghislaine Maxwell, owned the National Enquirer, Michels says, and he ties this to the shaping of UFO coverage in the 1980s, when, in his telling, the approach shifted from secrecy to flooding the public with stories. He raises it himself, also naming Rupert Murdoch, in a conversation with a UFO investigator named James Fox. If true, it would mean a tabloid's UFO stories were steered from above."
